# Unit13
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit13核心词汇

poverty/ˈpɑːvərti/贫困/Many people still live in poverty.
practical/ˈpræktɪkl/实际的/We need practical solutions, not theories.
precaution/prɪˈkɔːʃn/预防措施/We should take precautions against fire.
precede/prɪˈsiːd/在…之前/The meeting was preceded by a brief introduction.
precious/ˈpreʃəs/珍贵的/Water is a precious resource in this region.
precise/prɪˈsaɪs/精确的/Can you give me a more precise answer?
predict/prɪˈdɪkt/预测/It is difficult to predict the future.
predominant/prɪˈdɑːmɪnənt/占主导地位的/English is the predominant language in business.
prejudice/ˈpredʒudɪs/偏见/We should fight against racial prejudice.
preliminary/prɪˈlɪmɪneri/初步的/The preliminary results are very promising.
premise/ˈpremɪs/前提/The argument is based on a false premise.
preserve/prɪˈzɜːrv/保护/We must preserve our cultural heritage.
pressure/ˈpreʃər/压力/He is under a lot of work pressure.
prestige/preˈstiːʒ/声望/The university has great prestige.
presumably/prɪˈzuːməbli/大概/Presumably, he will arrive tomorrow.
prevail/prɪˈveɪl/盛行；获胜/Justice will prevail in the end.
previous/ˈpriːviəs/以前的/She had no previous experience in this field.
primarily/praɪˈmerəli/主要地/The book is primarily aimed at beginners.
prime/praɪm/主要的/He is in the prime of his life.
primitive/ˈprɪmɪtɪv/原始的/The tribe lives a primitive life.
principle/ˈprɪnsəpl/原则/He is a man of principle.
prior/ˈpraɪər/在先的/Prior to the meeting, please read the report.
priority/praɪˈɔːrəti/优先/Safety should be our top priority.
privilege/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒ/特权/It is a privilege to work with such talented people.
probe/proʊb/探查/Scientists sent a space probe to Mars.
proceed/proˈsiːd/继续/Please proceed with the next step.
process/ˈprɑːses/过程/Learning is a lifelong process.
profound/prəˈfaʊnd/深刻的/The book had a profound impact on me.
progressive/prəˈɡresɪv/进步的/She holds progressive political views.
prohibit/prəˈhɪbɪt/禁止/Smoking is prohibited in public areas.
project/ˈprɑːdʒekt/项目/The project was completed on time.
prominent/ˈprɑːmɪnənt/杰出的/He is a prominent scientist.
promote/prəˈmoʊt/促进；推广/The company promoted its new product aggressively.
prompt/prɑːmpt/迅速的；促使/The news prompted a heated debate.
propaganda/ˌprɑːpəˈɡændə/宣传/The government used propaganda to influence public opinion.
proportion/prəˈpɔːrʃn/比例/A large proportion of the population lives in cities.
propose/prəˈpoʊz/提议/He proposed a new plan for the project.
prospect/ˈprɑːspekt/前景/The prospects for economic growth are good.
prosperity/prɑːˈsperəti/繁荣/The country enjoyed a period of prosperity.
protest/ˈproʊtest/抗议/Thousands of people joined the protest.
prove/pruːv/证明/He proved his innocence with solid evidence.
provide/prəˈvaɪd/提供/The school provides free meals for students.
provoke/prəˈvoʊk/激怒/His remarks provoked anger among the audience.
pursue/pərˈsuː追求/He pursued his dream of becoming a doctor.
qualify/ˈkwɑːlɪfaɪ/有资格/She qualifies for the scholarship.
quote/kwoʊt/引用/He quoted a famous saying in his speech.
radical/ˈrædɪkl/激进的/The government proposed radical reforms.
rage/reɪdʒ/愤怒/He was filled with rage.
random/ˈrændəm/随机的/The numbers were selected at random.
range/reɪndʒ/范围/There is a wide range of products to choose from.
